            <ArticleTitle>Aberrant left coronary artery, modified unroofing technique, and patch angioplasty.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>508-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1540-8191.2010.01101.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">We present a case of surgical correction of an aberrant left coronary artery arising from the right sinus of Valsalva.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHOD" NlmCategory="METHODS">In order to prevent stenosis and kinking of the neo-ostium, modified unroofing technique was combined with patch angioplasty.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The clinical outcome was excellent with complete preservation of ventricular function, resolution of angina, and absence of aortic regurgitation.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Addition of patch angioplasty to the unroofing technique improves outcome.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2010 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
